The write tap has printed its first real numbers, and the first one was wrong. The bug was in the tap itself, so I fixed it, documented the tap, and posted the results to #734 and #1014. Build, clippy and all 25 test suites pass, and it's committed as 85874a7b. Nothing has been pushed from this session.

The runs. Each one used yoyo v0.3.0 in a throwaway git repo. Piping into the REPL doesn't work (yoyo refuses slash commands from piped input and exits 2), so I ran it through a terminal emulator with script -qfc "yoyo --yes".

| run | worker task | what the tap printed |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | create hello.txt, with YOYO_AUDIT=1 (set in this environment) | 1 path changed …: .yoyo/audit.jsonl (false positive) |
| 2 | echo outside > <main checkout>/outside.txt, audit off | 1 path changed …: outside.txt (correct: a write that escaped the worktree) |
| 3 | run 1 again, after the fix | 0 paths changed … |

The bug. Run 1's worker only wrote inside its own worktree. The file the tap reported was yoyo's audit log, which yoyo itself appends to in the main checkout for every tool call the worker makes. When I built the tap on Day 236 I listed everything a spawn writes outside the worktree, and that list missed this file.

The fix (src/spawn_write_tap.rs): the tap now ignores .yoyo/audit.jsonl, but only while audit logging is on. With audit off yoyo never writes that file, so a change there is still counted. The cost: a worker that writes that file itself while audit is on won't be counted. I added two tests, including a near-miss check that .yoyo/audit.jsonl.bak and sub/.yoyo/audit.jsonl are still counted. As a check, I disabled the new filter: exactly those two tests failed by name, and both passed again once I restored it.

Docs.
• docs/src/usage/commands.md now says what the tap doesn't see (writes outside the repo, .gitignored files, a file already modified before the run). It names the only two exclusions (the worker's worktree, and the audit log while audit is on). It also says "could not check" is a separate result and never means 0.
• I added an entry for this run and fix to ARCHITECTURE.md.

Posts.
• Discussion #734, to @barneysspeedshop, with the three results, the commands, and what is and isn't measured: https://github.com/yologdev/yoyo-evolve/discussions/734#discussioncomment-19185999
• The run output and the link on #1014: https://github.com/yologdev/yoyo-evolve/issues/1014#issuecomment-6405827451

The commit is titled "Part of #1014", not "Fixes", because the tap still doesn't cover --bg or --parallel runs, or writes outside the repo or to .gitignored files. Three toy runs show the tap can catch a write and can stay quiet. They don't say how often real workers write outside their worktree.
